  <wpt lat="41.126133" lon="-95.966933">
    <time>2026-09-19T08:30:00</time>
    <name>GCBVWZJ</name>
    <desc>CITO Across the World -  Bellevue, Nebraska USA by LadyCache, Cache In Trash Out Event (1.0/1.0)</desc>
    <url>https://coord.info/GCBVWZJ</url>
    <urlname>CITO Across the World -  Bellevue, Nebraska USA</urlname>
    <sym>Geocache</sym>
    <type>Geocache|Cache In Trash Out Event</type>
    <groundspeak:cache id="10549072" archived="False" available="True" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
      <groundspeak:name>CITO Across the World -  Bellevue, Nebraska USA</groundspeak:name>
      <groundspeak:placed_by>LadyCache</groundspeak:placed_by>
      <groundspeak:owner id="568858">LadyCache</groundspeak:owner>
      <groundspeak:type>Cache In Trash Out Event</groundspeak:type>
      <groundspeak:container>Other</groundspeak:container>
      <groundspeak:attributes>
        <groundspeak:attribute id="24" inc="1">Wheelchair accessible</groundspeak:attribute>
        <groundspeak:attribute id="6" inc="1">Recommended for kids</groundspeak:attribute>
        <groundspeak:attribute id="1" inc="1">Dogs</groundspeak:attribute>
        <groundspeak:attribute id="25" inc="1">Parking nearby</groundspeak:attribute>
      </groundspeak:attributes>
      <groundspeak:difficulty>1.0</groundspeak:difficulty>
      <groundspeak:terrain>1.0</groundspeak:terrain>
      <groundspeak:country>United States</groundspeak:country>
      <groundspeak:state>Nebraska</groundspeak:state>
      <groundspeak:short_description html="True">&lt;b&gt;19 September 2026, 08:30 - 09:30&lt;/b&gt;</groundspeak:short_description>
      <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;19 September 2026, 08:30 am - 9:30 am&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h1 style="text-align:center;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="background-color:#2ecc71;"&gt;CITO   CITO   CITO   CITO   CITO   CITO&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;

&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="text-align:center;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size:16px;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Come join the fun of picking up trash along 36th Street between Highway 370 and Capehart Road. &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="text-align:center;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size:16px;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This is the Fall &amp;#39;26 McEvoy CITO!!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="text-align:center;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size:16px;"&gt;We will meet at the posted coordinated in the parking lot at St Matthews Church for instructions and bags.  Please bring any gloves and pick up tools you prefer.  &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="text-align:center;"&gt; &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="text-align:center;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size:16px;"&gt;This stretch of road has paved sidewalks on both sides of the road in most places. Children must be under supervision of an adult for obvious safety precautions. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="text-align:center;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size:16px;"&gt;After instructions, the group can split up and I can shuttle cachers to the ends for the walk back to the parking lot. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="text-align:center;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size:24px;"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#2ecc71;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="background-color:#ffffff;"&gt;Group pictures at end of event.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The McEvoy family has had this stretch of adopt-a-road since 1999, with just one family member able to continue this great service.  I know he will appreciate us geocachers to participate with him.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="text-align:center;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size:24px;"&gt;One Day. Many Communities. A World of Difference.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="text-align:center;"&gt; &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size:14px;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What could happen if geocachers around the world came together on one day to make their communities cleaner?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size:14px;"&gt;In 2024, a Texan geocacher, Georeyna, came up with the idea to organize a series of CITO ® events held in conjunction with World Cleanup Day. Geocachers throughout Texas would host cleanup events in their own communities on the same day. While each event is locally organized, together they become part of something much bigger: CITO Across Texas was born! &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;span style="font-size:14px;"&gt;The results were tremendous. During 2024 and 2025:&lt;br /&gt;
• More than 50 CITO events were held across Texas.&lt;br /&gt;
• More than 700 volunteers participated.&lt;br /&gt;
• Thousands of pounds of trash were removed from parks, trails, waterways, neighborhoods, and other public spaces.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size:14px;"&gt;In 2026, they&amp;#39;re going bigger from CITO Across Texas to&lt;strong&gt; CITO Across the World!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size:14px;"&gt;The organizer, BE Viking, is hoping to have events hosted in all 50 states and at least 50 other countries. If you&amp;#39;d like to see more about this or would like to host an event, check out the website: &lt;a href="https://citoacrosstheworld.org/"&gt;CitoAcrosstheWorld&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size:14px;"&gt;I was thrilled to be asked to participate. The location is the approx mile between Highway 370 and Capehart Rd.  We&amp;#39;ve CITO&amp;#39;ed lots of trash here the past couple years and looking forward to seeing what we find this year.  Keep track of the most unusual CITO find again this year.  (Last year those pesky little bottles were counted as to how many we collected as well)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2 style="text-align:center;"&gt;&lt;img src="https://img.geocaching.com:443/3228c529-a555-49ab-93ae-88a39488b495.jpg" /&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p style="text-align:center;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size:22px;"&gt;One Day -- Every Time Zone&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="text-align:center;"&gt; &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="text-align:center;"&gt;&lt;img src="https://img.geocaching.com/eb86c82a-4088-4f54-9dab-ead2d30bb5dc.png" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="text-align:center;"&gt; &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="text-align:center;"&gt;&lt;a href="http://nebraskache.com/"&gt;&lt;img height="112" src="https://img.geocaching.com/9102f957-c986-41b5-acdb-a076bd017129.jpg" width="224" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="text-align:center;"&gt;&lt;a href="http://nebraskache.com/"&gt;Hosted By A Nebraskache Member&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="text-align:center;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.facebook.com/groups/107321656812/"&gt;&lt;img height="68" src="https://s3.amazonaws.com/gs-geo-images/19b6196d-f1d8-431b-9201-f4069d107ada_l.png" width="213" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="text-align:center;"&gt;As the geocache event owner, I ensure that these links to a local geocaching group that is active in the community and contributing to geocaching in positive ways. This link has not been checked by Geocaching HQ or by the reviewer.&lt;/p&gt;
</groundspeak:long_description>
